(The cost of curvature) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Forming the Hessian takes n^2 entries and solving the linear) Tj T*
(system takes about n^3 operations, which is too expensive when) Tj T*
(a model has millions of parameters.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Quasi-Newton methods such as BFGS build an approximation of the) Tj T*
(inverse Hessian from successive gradient differences. L-BFGS keeps) Tj T*
(only the last few difference pairs, so memory grows linearly in n.) Tj T*
ET
